BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wk14-str-tue@nyc-marathon-2026
DTSTAMP:20260802T120000Z
SEQUENCE:4
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260728T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Strength A — hamstrings/glutes/hips
DESCRIPTION:THIS WEEK: First week of Nordics: 2×3 only.\n\nSESSION A —
  heavy posterior chain (hamstrings/glutes/hips). ~40 min:\n1. Romanian d
 eadlift 3×8 (the #1 hamstring builder - hinge\, flat back\, feel the st
 retch)\n2. Nordic curl eccentrics - START 2×3\, build to 3×5 over 4 wk
 s (brutal DOMS when new: Tue ONLY\, never Thu)\n3. Bulgarian split squat
  3×8/leg (hip extension + quad eccentric - doubles as TMB descent prep)
 \n4. Single-leg hip thrust 3×10/leg (glute max - fixes the underused po
 sterior chain in your gait)\n5. Calf raises 3×12 straight-knee + 3×12 
 bent-knee (Achilles insurance for the volume ramp)\n6. Copenhagen side p
 lank 2×20s/side (adductors - overlooked running stabiliser)\n\nDo 4-6+ 
 hrs after the morning club session. Skip anything that alters your gait 
 next day.
CATEGORIES:Training,Strength
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wk14-str-thu@nyc-marathon-2026
DTSTAMP:20260802T120000Z
SEQUENCE:4
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260730T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Strength B — hamstrings/glutes/hips
DESCRIPTION:SESSION B — moderate\, gait + stability (NO heavy eccentric
 s: long run is ~36 hrs away). ~35 min:\n1. Barbell or single-leg hip thr
 ust 3×10 (moderate load)\n2. Step-downs slow 3×8/leg (eccentric quad c
 ontrol - TMB descent prep + knee tracking)\n3. Hamstring bridge walkouts
  or swiss-ball curls 3×8 (hamstring endurance\, low DOMS)\n4. Banded st
 anding hip-flexor march 3×10/leg (hip flexors need STRENGTH too\, not j
 ust stretching - weak+tight is the usual combo)\n5. Lateral band walks 2
 ×15/side + clamshells 2×15 (glute med - single-leg stance stability)\n
 6. Plank 2×45s + side plank 2×30s/side\n\nDo 4-6+ hrs after the mornin
 g club tempo. Moderate effort - leave the gym feeling worked\, not wreck
 ed.
CATEGORIES:Training,Strength
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
