BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wk19-str-tue@nyc-marathon-2026
DTSTAMP:20260802T120000Z
SEQUENCE:4
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260901T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Strength A — hamstrings/glutes/hips
DESCRIPTION:THIS WEEK: Last heavy Session A before TMB.\n\nSESSION A — 
 heavy posterior chain (hamstrings/glutes/hips). ~40 min:\n1. Romanian de
 adlift 3×8 (the #1 hamstring builder - hinge\, flat back\, feel the str
 etch)\n2. Nordic curl eccentrics - START 2×3\, build to 3×5 over 4 wks
  (brutal DOMS when new: Tue ONLY\, never Thu)\n3. Bulgarian split squat 
 3×8/leg (hip extension + quad eccentric - doubles as TMB descent prep)\
 n4. Single-leg hip thrust 3×10/leg (glute max - fixes the underused pos
 terior chain in your gait)\n5. Calf raises 3×12 straight-knee + 3×12 b
 ent-knee (Achilles insurance for the volume ramp)\n6. Copenhagen side pl
 ank 2×20s/side (adductors - overlooked running stabiliser)\n\nDo 4-6+ h
 rs after the morning club session. Skip anything that alters your gait n
 ext day.
CATEGORIES:Training,Strength
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wk19-str-thu@nyc-marathon-2026
DTSTAMP:20260802T120000Z
SEQUENCE:4
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260903T184500
SUMMARY:🏋️ Strength B — hamstrings/glutes/hips
DESCRIPTION:THIS WEEK: Light version - peak LR in ~36 hrs.\n\nSESSION B 
 — moderate\, gait + stability (NO heavy eccentrics: long run is ~36 hr
 s away). ~35 min:\n1. Barbell or single-leg hip thrust 3×10 (moderate l
 oad)\n2. Step-downs slow 3×8/leg (eccentric quad control - TMB descent 
 prep + knee tracking)\n3. Hamstring bridge walkouts or swiss-ball curls 
 3×8 (hamstring endurance\, low DOMS)\n4. Banded standing hip-flexor mar
 ch 3×10/leg (hip flexors need STRENGTH too\, not just stretching - weak
 +tight is the usual combo)\n5. Lateral band walks 2×15/side + clamshell
 s 2×15 (glute med - single-leg stance stability)\n6. Plank 2×45s + sid
 e plank 2×30s/side\n\nDo 4-6+ hrs after the morning club tempo. Moderat
 e effort - leave the gym feeling worked\, not wrecked.
CATEGORIES:Training,Strength
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
